# Transcript actor rails and active presence

`Transcript` now paints one semantic rail per block instead of relying on a
kind-colored prefix alone. Active blocks can animate that rail from a
host-owned deterministic tick. Folded Thinking blocks preview up to three
lines; other folded kinds remain one row.

## API edits

External `TranscriptBlock` struct literals must add `active`, or migrate to
the constructor and builder:

```rust
let block = TranscriptBlock::new(id, TranscriptKind::Assistant, &lines)
    .active(streaming);
let transcript = Transcript::new(&blocks, &system).tick(frame_tick);
```

Actor mapping is now User→`ActorUser`, Assistant→`ActorAssistant`,
Thinking→`ActorThinking`, Tool→`ActorTool`, Approval→`ActorPlan`, and
System→`ActorSystem`. Reduced motion keeps active rails static and identical
across ticks.

Delete consumer-owned transcript gutters, actor color maps, and streaming
rail animation. Do not retain parallel paint paths.

